%% Inline formatting and smart typography.
%%   lmr2svg examples/formatting/deck.lmr -o formatting.html
!title Text formatting

!slide Inline styles

The four doubled markers: **bold**, __italic__, ~~strikethrough~~, ++underline++.

They compose: **__bold italic__**, and each has a class fallback for use with
other attributes, e.g. [important]{.bold #c0392b} (bold + red).

!slide Spans and smart typography

A span carries a `{…}` attribute: [a colour]{#1c6fb0}, [a tint]{bg:#dde8ff},
[a named class]{.bold}. It is *not* a formatting language — only names and hints.

Smart typography educates plain ASCII on every prose run: en dash (pages 3--5),
em dash (asides---like this), ellipsis (and so on...), and quotes that curl by
context ("quoted", don't, the '90s). Code and $math$ are left verbatim.

!slide Styled blocks

!style[.center .frame bg:#f5f7ff]
	`!style[.frame bg:…]` wraps a whole block in a rounded, tinted panel.

	It can hold any content, including display maths: $E = mc^2$.
